# ============================================================================
# deploy/terraform/.gitignore — keep Terraform working files OUT of git
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The parent deploy/.gitignore also covers these, but this local copy makes the
# rule obvious to anyone working inside deploy/terraform/ and survives if the
# directory is ever copied/zipped on its own (e.g. uploaded into CloudShell).
#
# WHY each is ignored:
#   .terraform/          provider plugins + module cache — re-created by `init`.
#   *.tfstate*           STATE. Holds resource IDs, secret ARNs, the generated
#                        RDS master password. MUST live in the S3 remote backend,
#                        NEVER in git. (See the backend "s3" stub in versions.tf.)
#   terraform.tfvars     sizing/topology chosen per-environment; may hint at
#                        internal CIDRs/handles. Copy from terraform.tfvars.example.
#   crash.log / *.tfplan generated artifacts, not source.
# ============================================================================

.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
terraform.tfvars
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan
tf.plan
